---
/** Code-owned Terms of Use. */

import LegalPage from "../layouts/LegalPage.astro";
import siteConfig, { formatPageTitle } from "../data/siteConfig";

const title = formatPageTitle("Terms of Use");
const description = `The terms that govern use of ${siteConfig.bandNameFormal}'s website.`;
const email = siteConfig.contact.email;
---

<LegalPage
  title={title}
  description={description}
  kicker="Legal"
  heading="Terms of Use"
  effectiveDate="September 11, 2026"
>
  <p>
    These Terms of Use govern your use of this website, operated by The Electric Lavender Train
    (“we,” “us,” or “our”). By using this website, you agree to these terms.
  </p>

  <h2>Informational use</h2>
  <p>
    This website is provided for informational purposes — to share information about The Electric
    Lavender Train, our music, upcoming and past shows, photos and video, merchandise, and how to
    reach us. It also links to a newsletter signup and unsubscribe form, and to forms for
    booking/merchandise/general inquiries, content removal requests, and testimonial submissions.
  </p>

  <h2>Booking inquiries are not a confirmed booking</h2>
  <p>
    Submitting the Booking Inquiry form, or contacting us by email, does not create a confirmed
    booking, reservation, or contract of any kind. A booking is confirmed only once we and you have
    entered into a separate written agreement covering the details of the event, and any required
    payment has been made under the terms of that agreement. Nothing on this website should be
    relied upon as a guarantee of availability or a confirmed engagement until that has happened.
  </p>

  <h2>Merchandise inquiries are not purchases</h2>
  <p>
    This website does not have an online store, shopping cart, or checkout. Submitting the Merch
    Inquiry form is a request for information — it is not a purchase, an order, or a payment
    transaction, and it does not obligate either party to complete a sale. Please do not submit
    payment card numbers or other payment information through any form on this website; we do not
    request or accept payment information this way.
  </p>

  <h2>Music page links are not audio hosting</h2>
  <p>
    The <a href={siteConfig.routes.music}>Music</a> page may link out to streaming platforms,
    pre-save pages, or a video for a given release. This website does not itself host, stream, sell,
    or distribute any audio — clicking a link there sends you to a separate, third-party destination
    described below.
  </p>

  <h2>Newsletter</h2>
  <p>
    When available, the optional newsletter link opens our email provider's hosted signup page,
    and a separate hosted unsubscribe form lets you opt out. Use of either page is also governed
    by the provider's terms and is described in our
    <a href={siteConfig.routes.privacy}>Privacy Policy</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>Event media submissions</h2>
  <p>
    When the Gallery &amp; Merchandise page offers a “Share Your Event Media” link, it opens a
    separate Google Form. The form presents the consent and license terms that apply to your
    submission; the points below summarize the site's operating boundaries and do not replace the
    form's terms:
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li>By submitting media, you confirm you actually took it, or otherwise have the authority to submit it to us for the uses described below.</li>
    <li>
      We may use submitted media only within the ordinary scope of promoting Electric
      Lavender Train — this website, our own social media accounts, and similar band promotion. We
      will not use it for paid advertising, on merchandise, for resale, or for promoting
      any artist or project unrelated to Electric Lavender Train (including other Heavy Crush
      Records artists) unless we separately ask for and receive your specific approval for that
      additional use.
    </li>
    <li>Submitting media does not guarantee we will publish it. We may decline to use any submission.</li>
    <li>
      If your submission includes other identifiable people, or any minor, we may need additional
      permission before using it, and may decline to publish it without that permission.
    </li>
    <li>
      If you'd like something you submitted taken down, use the Content Removal Request form on the
      <a href={siteConfig.routes.contactBooking}>Contact & Booking</a> page. Submitting that request
      starts our review — it does not automatically guarantee removal.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Testimonial submissions</h2>
  <p>
    When the About page offers a testimonial submission link, it opens a separate Google Form. The
    form presents the consent and permission terms that apply to your submission; the points below
    summarize the site's operating boundaries and do not replace the form's terms:
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li>
      By submitting a testimonial, you confirm it truthfully describes your own first-hand
      experience with Electric Lavender Train, and that you have the authority to submit it and
      any accompanying material to us.
    </li>
    <li>
      We may publish your testimonial only with the public attribution you selected in the form
      (including anonymously or with a first name only, if that is what you chose).
    </li>
    <li>
      We may make minor, non-material edits to a submitted testimonial for length or clarity, but
      only where the form asks for and you give that consent — we will not change its meaning or
      attribute a statement to you that you did not make.
    </li>
    <li>Submitting a testimonial does not guarantee we will publish it. We may decline to use any submission.</li>
    <li>
      If you'd like a published testimonial removed or corrected, use the Content Removal Request
      form on the <a href={siteConfig.routes.contactBooking}>Contact & Booking</a> page. Submitting
      that request starts our review — it does not automatically guarantee removal.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Permitted use</h2>
  <p>You may use this website for its intended informational and inquiry purposes. You agree not to:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>Use this website for any unlawful purpose;</li>
    <li>Attempt to gain unauthorized access to this website or its underlying systems;</li>
    <li>Submit false, abusive, or malicious content through any form on this site; or</li>
    <li>Use automated means to scrape, spam, or overload this website or its forms.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Ownership of content</h2>
  <p>
    Content on this website — including text, photographs, video, music, logos, and artwork — may
    be owned by, or licensed to, The Electric Lavender Train. You may not reproduce, distribute, or
    otherwise use content from this website beyond ordinary browsing without our permission, except
    as permitted by applicable law.
  </p>

  <h2>Our relationship with Heavy Crush Records</h2>
  <p>
    The Electric Lavender Train is part of Heavy Crush Records. This website is dedicated to
    Electric Lavender Train; it is not a promotional site for Heavy Crush Records or its other
    artists, and any acknowledgment of that relationship on this site is informational, not an
    endorsement or promotion of unrelated acts.
  </p>

  <h2>Third-party links and embedded services</h2>
  <p>
    This website links to and embeds content from third-party services, which may include music
    streaming and pre-save platforms, social media platforms, Brevo (our newsletter provider),
    Google Forms (for event-media and testimonial submissions), and YouTube. Those services each have their own
    terms of use and privacy policies, which are not controlled by us and which you should review
    separately before using them. We are not responsible for the content, availability, security, or
    practices of any third-party service, and linking to one is not an endorsement of everything on
    it.
  </p>

  <h2>Disclaimers</h2>
  <p>
    This website and its content are provided “as is,” without warranties of any kind, to the
    extent permitted by law. We do not guarantee that this website will be uninterrupted,
    error-free, or completely secure. Information on this website (including show dates,
    availability, and release details) may change and may not always be current.
  </p>

  <h2>Limitation of liability</h2>
  <p>
    To the extent permitted by law, The Electric Lavender Train is not liable for any indirect,
    incidental, or consequential damages arising from your use of this website. Nothing in these
    Terms is intended to limit any liability that cannot be limited under applicable law.
  </p>

  <h2>Changes to these Terms</h2>
  <p>
    We may update these Terms of Use from time to time. Material changes will be reflected by
    updating the effective date at the top of this page. Continued use of this website after a
    change means you accept the updated Terms.
  </p>

  <h2>Contact us</h2>
  <p>
    Questions about these Terms of Use can be sent to <a href={`mailto:${email}`}>{email}</a>.
  </p>
</LegalPage>
